  "story": "The campers at a summer camp are numbered from 0 and arrive as strangers; people is how many there are. Friendships are made one after another: friendship k joins camper a[k] and camper b[k]. Friends of friends belong to the same group, and a camper without friends is a group of one. After each friendship, how many separate groups are there? Return the list of those counts. A big camp must be finished within the operation budget: recounting, or renaming a whole group at every friendship, is too slow, and so is a long walk to a group's leader at every friendship.",
  "io": {
    "inputs": [
      {"name": "people", "type": "num"},
      {"name": "a", "type": "array<num>"},
      {"name": "b", "type": "array<num>"}
    ],
    "output": {"type": "array<num>"}
  },
  "constraints": {
    "n": {"min": 0, "max": 1800},
    "notes": ["1 to 1200 campers and 0 to 1800 friendships.", "a and b have the same length; nobody befriends themself.", "The same two campers may be listed more than once."]
  },
  "blocks": {
